WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.960
A NETFLIX ORIGINAL SERIES

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:26.900
Hey. Do you remember that time
Mel made some bread that was so hard,

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.150
it chipped Grandpa's tooth?

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:31.030
Oh, yeah.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.610
I've never seen Grandpa so panicked.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.070
He had tears in his eyes...

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.030
But...

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.080
the bread Mel made was always delicious.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:43.830
Yeah.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.750
We would all eat it together...

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.550
I wanted us all to always be...

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.420
For us all to...

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:49.210
The Song of Departure

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.710
I don't have anything either.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.430
I'm not lying.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.060
I can't take this anymore.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.600
Me neither.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.480
Hey, you!

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.940
This is bad!

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.280
Someone! Help!

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.830
You walked all the way
from Dandela Village? That's crazy.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.250
Go ahead and eat as much as you want.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.050
Thank you. I'll have seconds.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:39.380
Hold on! Control yourself!

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.220
No problem.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:42.720
Just a second.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.180
Their village was burned down.
Maybe it was a Minstrel Hunt.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.390
What's that?

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.940
I heard soldiers of the Capital Army

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.860
are capturing people
who are involved with songs.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:01.280
I can't believe there was a singer
in the countryside.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.700
What if...?

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.370
Don't worry about it. Enjoy your meal.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:30.680
So, it really did happen because
I didn't obey Grandpa and sang a song.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.680
It's my fault.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:33.980
No!

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:38.650
Hey, you saved Leobolt,
that knight from the Capital, right?

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.360
<i>And Mel always said that...</i>

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.650
<i>your songs cheer people up.</i>

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.870
You're going to the Capital to sing.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.830
You promised Mel.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.580
Keep your spirits up.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.250
Al...

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.000
What?! You're not going to pay?

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.630
A spider entered my bedroom last night.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.880
That means I spent the whole night
with a spider.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.840
I can't get married anymore.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.890
-Make it up to me.
-How am I to do that?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:15.140
Not paying for the room
because of one bug? Unacceptable.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.230
I wasn't planning on saying this, but...

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:26.400
I'm a Court Minstrel
who used to serve the Capital.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:28.370
I'm Pony Goodlight.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.830
I'm hiding my identity right now
for personal reasons.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.080
Al, did you hear that?

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:35.960
She's from the Capital.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:39.790
A Court Minstrel?
She's an important person.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.130
Why is she alone in a place like this?

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.190
Leobolt!

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:10.700
Crette.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.120
You're back already.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.080
How were the feudal lords
in the countryside?

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:21.670
Things are complicated.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.710
The fighting has already started.

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:26.760
Were you okay?

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:27.670
Yeah.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.640
But... some innocent villagers
got caught up in the fighting.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:33.640
It can't be helped.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.560
Several countries are trying
to attack our Capital,

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.150
to get their hands on our songstress.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.400
An army healed by a song's power,

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:45.480
no matter how much they fight
and get injured,

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.610
is most powerful.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.700
She's not a tool for war.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.120
You're too kind.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.460
The crest of Leobolt is crying!

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.380
The Crette family is leaving
the Capital today!

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.340
We will suppress the fighting
on the border!

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.550
Our crest shall go down in history,
Leobolt!

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:14.550
Crette...

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:21.100
I wish all the fighting...

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.850
would disappear.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.030
Miss Finis.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:36.490
You'll catch a cold. Come inside.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.080
I'm not that frail.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.580
Let's go to the castle town
and buy some flowers instead.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.630
It's forbidden for you
to leave the palace.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:50.170
Even if you did go to the castle town,
you'd get lost right away.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.470
I won't get lost.

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.800
The roads change on their own.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:58.100
They used to be like this,
but now they're like this...

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.730
They haven't changed
for hundreds of years.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.560
If you go out and get hurt,

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.940
Prince Rudo will be saddened.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:06.860
Come.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.780
You don't understand.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:13.240
Look, I'm not clumsy at all.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.080
Ouch...

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.160
Huh? Corte?

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:21.870
Where are you, Corte?

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.250
No way. Did she disappear?

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.250
I'm here!

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.590
Don't say, "Ah!"

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:33.470
I can't believe this.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.760
Are you hurt?

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.180
I'm fine.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:45.190
You're much more valuable
than you realize.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.110
Prince Rudo!

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:55.030
Thanks to Miss Finis's song the other day,

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.700
the morale of the Army is much higher,

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:01.450
and they won a string of battles
at the border!

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.290
The power of her song is amazing.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.130
And she's very popular with the people.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:10.170
I'm sure she's a goddess of victory.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.590
That's why she's my future wife.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.550
The Capital is safe.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:16.970
Yes.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:22.100
My daughter said that Miss Finis's
singing voice saved her life.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:24.100
I see, I see.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:28.020
Although, my daughter said
that we also may have put

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.570
too many constraints on Miss Finis.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.150
She's always in that tower...

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.400
Are you dissatisfied with my methods?

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.870
No! That's not what I meant.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.830
You have not been properly educated.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:56.720
However, it might be a good idea
to let her have some fun

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.680
while she still can.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:00.850
Then we shall do so!

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.350
We still have other ways to use Finis.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:25.450
Will we get to the Capital
if we follow her?

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.000
Who knows?

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.960
She looks a little suspicious.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.340
Well, that's how it is.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:34.920
Excuse me.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.010
That will be 120 gold pieces.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:38.260
What?!

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.390
Your identity won't change the fee.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:43.430
Are you crazy?
You're taking money from a customer!

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:44.510
It's Default!

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:46.890
Then let's do this.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:51.440
If this coin comes up heads,
then the room is free.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.400
If it's tails, I'll pay half.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:56.190
Why is the maximum only half?!

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:02.070
Hey, hey, hey!

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:07.330
-You're so stubborn.
-One hundred and 20 gold pieces!

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:09.250
You're a horrible man.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:11.460
One hundred and 20 gold pieces!

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:13.790
Hey, hey! Court Minstrel!

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.460
You're from the Capital, right?

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:19.300
Then you know how to get
to the Capital, right?

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:20.800
Of course.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:24.350
I'm a beautiful Court Minstrel

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:27.140
who used to serve at the Capital.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:30.810
Most people don't
call themselves beautiful...

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.400
It doesn't really matter.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:35.520
Old man, I want to talk to her.
Can you wrap it up?

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:38.650
-I'm going to have her pay.
-I'm not going to pay.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:39.990
Come on.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:41.950
I got it.

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:44.820
You're a Court Minstrel, right?

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:48.410
If you sing for me,
I'll make your room free.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.000
All she has to do is sing?

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.460
If she really is a Court Minstrel,

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.500
then her songs have tremendous value.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:58.840
You're a smart kid.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:03.300
I'm a genius scientist
who will be famous in the Capital.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.930
Most people don't
call themselves a genius...

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:09.020
You're one to talk!

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:11.980
Well... Okay.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:14.520
I'll sing.

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.400
Did you call for me, Your Highness?

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:25.570
The prince seems to be up to something.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:28.870
What's going on, General Bazra?

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:34.580
It must be the clash near the border
with Granadia, the neighboring country.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:39.550
They must have noticed Finis.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.590
They're pretty sharp.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:47.180
We should tighten our guard around
the songstress as a countermeasure.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:53.180
Finis is the key to winning this war.

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.560
That's right.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:05.660
Keep looking for the girl who sings.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.910
-She should still be in the countryside.
-Yes, sir!

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.790
Court Minstrels and small Orchestras.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.460
-Don't overlook any details!
-Yes, sir!

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:19.880
There's more than one key to this war.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:22.210
General Bazra.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:27.340
As ordered, we've tightened the guard
at the checkpoints.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:28.640
Thank you.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:30.970
What about Leobolt?

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:34.310
He definitely opposes the war.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:37.600
He's up to something unsettling,

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:39.860
but we're not sure what it is yet.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:43.530
If only we had killed him
in that forest...

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:45.320
He's from a distinguished family.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:48.490
Killing him in the open
would be difficult...

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:49.740
That's enough.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:52.910
Be on the lookout for him
at the checkpoint.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:55.660
And continue the manhunt
for the girl who sings.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:58.370
Where are you going?

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:00.630
To Ash City.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.300
The Star Song Festival is approaching!

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:20.360
The smell of the earth,
the smell of the wind,

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:21.980
and the smell of the sky!

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:23.230
This is wonderful!

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.780
The sky doesn't have any smell.

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:27.450
It does!

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:34.200
She's so excited just by gaining
permission to go for a walk.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:35.410
Right.

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:39.830
But getting to spend time like this
is really special for Miss Finis.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.920
So, I want to let her do
whatever she wants.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:44.840
You have a hard life, Corte.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.050
I'm always in that tower.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:49.630
And Prince Rudo visits often.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:53.220
You don't know about the knight
who visited the palace, then?

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:54.810
The handsome knight.

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:57.810
What? I haven't heard anything!
From which family?

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:03.110
-I heard he's from a distinguished family.
-A distinguished family?! Really?!

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.370
-Um...
-Yes!

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.920
Excuse me. I seem to be lost.

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:25.000
Which way is the Path of the Sun?

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:26.960
The Path of the Sun?

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.840
It's on the other side of this wall.

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:32.180
But men are forbidden to enter.

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:36.310
Yes. I've been assigned to be a guard
since the war is approaching.

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:37.470
Thank you.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.680
A guard? For who?

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.100
Excuse me.

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:47.280
That's the Crette family crest...

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:53.410
I'm lost again.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.200
Did I come this way?

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:57.410
Or was it that way?

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:59.790
-There you are.
-Huh?

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.410
This place is...

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:04.750
Forbidden to men. I know.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:08.460
I've come to guard you,
on orders of Prince Rudo.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.010
From Prince Rudo?

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:15.090
Keeping you inside all the time
isn't fair,

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:19.430
so he said you're permitted to go out
as far as the city. Come this way.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:21.640
Where are my attendants?

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.690
Going in a large group
would draw attention.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:26.860
That crest...

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:31.190
So, you've returned. I thought
you'd only just left the Capital.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:33.860
Yes. That's right.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:35.410
Miss Finis!

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.240
You're from the Leobolt family... Henry!

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.080
I'm deeply honored
that you remember me.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.670
Thank you for earlier, Leobolt.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:48.540
We're in a hurry to be on our way...

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.380
Where are you going?

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:55.470
It's an order from Prince Rudo.
I can't tell you the details.

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:56.930
Forgive me.

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:01.600
Your crest tells me
that you're from the Marlle family.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.350
Yes, that's right.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:05.310
-The Marlle family--
-Impostor!

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.400
That crest is of the Crette family!

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.360
You're not from this country!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:22.250
Are you okay?

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.500
I can't breathe...

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:26.460
Are you hurt?

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:28.830
You're holding too tight...

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:30.920
Forgive me.

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.550
This is no good!

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:43.060
-Are you hurt?
-I'm fine.

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.020
What about you?

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:46.810
I'm fine.

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:49.480
I'm glad you're safe, Leobolt.

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:00.200
So, you do have money!

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.290
I have lots of money.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:06.460
But I don't want to pay any gold pieces
for that kind of service.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:09.790
What a huge grudge for one spider.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:14.170
But are you really okay with this?
There may be a Minstrel Hunt...

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:17.260
I sing when I want to.

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:19.430
I sing because it's fun.

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:21.800
There's no other reason.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:30.690
But you're singing in exchange
for the room fee.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:46.120
<i>The country where eternity is woven</i>

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:50.460
<i>Thy name is</i>

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:54.210
<i>Golt, Golt</i>

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:58.590
<i>The land of gold</i>

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:03.720
<i>Spilt blood shows courage and beauty</i>

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:07.100
Why do we have to assign that man
to be Finis's guard?

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:08.730
<i>For us who are filled with pride</i>

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:10.520
He won the swordsmanship competition

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:13.900
and is the hero who saved Miss Finis
from the assassin.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:18.150
The people admire him.
We're just making good use of him.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:23.370
<i>Spread pure white wings of Justice</i>

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:26.950
<i>And leadeth everything</i>

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:30.750
<i>The country of destiny</i>

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:34.840
<i>Golt, Golt</i>

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:36.880
<i>Live together...</i>

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.460
<i>Henry Leobolt.</i>

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:42.970
I appoint you
as Finis's guardian knight.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:46.220
Offer your services to my future wife.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:47.430
Yes, sir!

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.430
<i>Miracles shine brightly...</i>

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:53.190
If Finis suffers even a single scratch,
consider yourself dead.

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:55.770
<i>Under the honorable flag</i>

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:56.730
Yes, sir!

00:19:57.440 --> 00:20:02.280
<i>The light that shines eternally</i>
<i>Shalt become a symbol...</i>

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:04.410
Our songstress of victory...

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:06.240
I shall...

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.450
protect you with my life.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:10.910
<i>The country where eternity is woven</i>

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:15.580
<i>We shall sing praises</i>

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:19.210
<i>And glorify thy name</i>

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:24.340
<i>Golt</i>

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:31.680
What a surprise! That was amazing!

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:33.480
The room is free!

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.100
What a good host!

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:38.610
You became such a good man.
I almost didn't recognize you.

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:41.030
Al.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.400
Thanks.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:44.740
I...

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.530
I'm fine now.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:54.500
That girl, she sings well.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:56.250
Thank you.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.040
I feel better because of your song.

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:00.550
I'm glad.

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:03.920
What is she doing?

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:05.760
Who knows.

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.850
The spirits aren't here...

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:17.190
What do you mean? Spirits?

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.650
You know. They come when I sing
the Song of Healing.

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:22.780
They have a beautiful glow...

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:25.280
No, that's scientifically...

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.820
You know how to sing the Song of Spirits?

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:30.450
The Song of Spirits?

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:38.290
It's a song from the ancient legends.

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:42.880
When a certain person sings it,
mysterious powers are born.

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:45.220
This...

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.930
Grandpa had one, too.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:53.390
Capital soldiers!
They've come on a Minstrel Hunt!

00:21:57.770 --> 00:21:58.770
This is strange.

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:00.820
The timing is too good.

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.610
Hey. It's her, right?

00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:06.150
Good job.

00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:11.160
Thanks.

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:18.710
The old lady?
